{{!
    @template tool_vae/pieces

    The supporting pieces of a declaration: one sentence when there is none, or the list (for each piece its nature, its
    title, its details; removed and when, or what the signature says of it and how to get at it: the address and its
    host, the file, or the word that the reader may not open it; whether the reader opened it; the button to remove it),
    then, for a reader who is not the vaeiste, how many files they opened. The parts of a piece touch, with nothing
    between them: a comment carries each line break inside the list.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\pieces. The template holds no logic. Every text
    and address is escaped (double braces). One key is HTML (triple braces): actionhtml, the button to remove a piece,
    made by the core ($output->single_button()).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * none - false, or a string: the sentence drawn when there is no piece
    * haspieces - bool, whether there is a list
    * pieces - array, each:
        * nature - string; title - false or {text}; details - string
        * removed - false, or {text, after}: when it was removed; after: false or {text}, covered by the signature
        * active - false, or {after, listonly, link, file, opened, actionhtml}: after - false or {text}, added after the
          signature; listonly - false or {text}; link - false or {url, host, open}; file - false or {url, open}; opened -
          false or {text}; actionhtml - false or HTML
    * count - false, or {text}: how many files the reader opened

    Example context (json):
    {
        "none": false,
        "haspieces": true,
        "pieces": [
            {"nature": "Diploma", "title": {"text": "Diplôme"}, "details": "20 November 2026, 10:00", "removed": false,
                "active": {"after": false, "listonly": false, "file": false, "opened": false, "actionhtml": false,
                    "link": {"url": "https://example.com/a", "host": "example.com", "open": "Open the link"} } },
            {"nature": "Contract", "title": false, "details": "PDF, 1KB", "active": false,
                "removed": {"text": "Removed on 20 November 2026.", "after": false} }
        ],
        "count": {"text": "0 of 0 files you may open were opened by you. Opening is not reading."}
    }
}}
{{#none}}
<p>{{none}}</p>
{{/none}}
{{#haspieces}}
<ul class="list-unstyled tool-vae-pieces">{{#pieces}}<li class="mb-3 tool-vae-piece"><strong>{{nature}}</strong>{{!
}}{{#title}} - {{text}}{{/title}}<div class="text-muted small">{{details}}</div>{{!
}}{{#removed}}<div class="text-muted">{{text}}</div>{{#after}}<div class="text-muted">{{text}}</div>{{/after}}{{/removed}}{{!
}}{{#active}}{{#after}}<div class="alert alert-warning py-1">{{text}}</div>{{/after}}{{!
}}{{#listonly}}<div class="text-muted">{{text}}</div>{{/listonly}}{{!
}}{{#link}}<div>{{url}}</div><div class="text-muted small">{{host}}</div>{{!
}}<div><a href="{{url}}" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">{{open}}</a></div>{{/link}}{{!
}}{{#file}}<div><a href="{{url}}">{{open}}</a></div>{{/file}}{{!
}}{{#opened}}<div class="text-muted small">{{text}}</div>{{/opened}}{{!
}}{{#actionhtml}}{{{actionhtml}}}{{/actionhtml}}{{/active}}</li>{{/pieces}}</ul>
{{#count}}
<p class="text-muted small">{{text}}</p>
{{/count}}
{{/haspieces}}
